// Terrain properties (design §3.1). Every terrain must be listed.
//
// A walkable terrain gives its step cost (what an orthogonal step onto it
// costs; a diagonal step costs 14/10 of that), its fertility (0 to 1) and
// whether sprites can drink there, and whether a fixture (such as a bush) may
// stand there. An unwalkable terrain gives only `walkable: false`.
//
// Any terrain may give `sound`: how much a call weakens crossing a tile of
// it, as a step's cost is for walking (M2 design §15.1). A call is heard
// wherever its way there costs at most `calls.reach` in physiology.ron. A
// terrain with none, rock here, stops calls.
{
    grass:         (walkable: true, step_cost: 10, fertility: 1.0, drinkable: false, allows_fixtures: true,  sound: 10),
    dirt:          (walkable: true, step_cost: 10, fertility: 0.5, drinkable: false, allows_fixtures: true,  sound: 10),
    sand:          (walkable: true, step_cost: 15, fertility: 0.0, drinkable: false, allows_fixtures: true,  sound: 10),
    shallow_water: (walkable: true, step_cost: 25, fertility: 0.0, drinkable: true,  allows_fixtures: false, sound: 10),
    deep_water:    (walkable: false, sound: 10),
    rock:          (walkable: false),
}
